rmers.\n- Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n- Utilities are 62% of orders at VLTX holdings. Pellham and Norvane together make up 56% of those utility orders.\n- Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 2026, to 165bp. Two utility share offerings were cut back in size. Norvane still priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably, so debt funding is still open. Tighter funding could delay the plans.\n\n**Data centres** (n8.r1)\n- Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027. That is slower than in 2026, because power availability limits new sites.\n- Demand is still rising, but the growth rate is slowing.\n\n**Caveats**\n- I found no order, backlog or delivery data.\n- The utility evidence names only Pellham and Norvane.\n- The 18%, 12% and 9% figures are plans or forecasts, not commitments.\n- The 9% figure is for connection requests, not equipment orders. Power constraints could stop some requests from becoming orders.\n- No source says how much of the utility capex is driven by data centres. The link from data-centre growth to equipment demand is inferred.\n- I don't know whether the capex figures are nominal or adjusted for inflation.","ttft_ms":7583,"type":"result","duration_ms":43808,"uuid":"be0d27e9-34ad-4218-ab6c-ec883bbe6e99","ttft_stream_ms":6630,"time_to_request_ms":469,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":34,"system_prompt":44,"resume_other":19,"process_user_input":42,"input_attachments":145,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":32,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":27,"init_frame_send":10,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":9,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":20,"request_announcements":29,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":20,"message_normalization":5,"client_creation":8,"request_build":18},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":229,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":126,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":185